# ── Non-production working files ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything that is not a shipped page or asset lives under _dev/ (archive,
# prototypes, reference, templates, tools, scratch). One rule replaces the
# forty-odd per-file entries this list used to carry: a new prototype or
# throwaway script needs no .gitignore edit, it just has to be created in the
# right folder. See _dev/README.md.
#
# serve.mjs still resolves those pages at their original root URL, so ignoring
# the folder costs nothing in local review.
_dev/

# Pages built but not yet routed for deploy. They live at the root because
# they are production-intent, not experiments; drop the entry once the page
# is wired into vercel.json.
buyers.html
brokers.html
developers.html
brand-partners.html
videoworks.html
videoworks.css
videoworks.js

# Editor / OS backups. Belt and braces: these belong in _dev/archive/, but a
# stray one at the root must not slip into a commit either.
*.bak
*.html.bak
*-backup.html
*-backup.js
*-backup.css

# Unused media takes
videoworks-hero1.mp4

.vercel
